  "verbalization": "Minaprine is shown to interact with Htr2c, which in turn participates in multiple binding processes, including serotonin and 1-(4-iodo-2,5-dimethoxyphenyl)propan-2-amine binding. These binding events are linked to Htr2a, suggesting a potential mechanism by which Minaprine influences Htr2a through its interaction with Htr2c. The evidence indicates that Minaprine may modulate Htr2a via a pathway involving Htr2c, possibly by altering the binding affinity or activity of Htr2c, which in turn affects Htr2a. The overlapping roles of Htr2c in different binding contexts highlight a possible functional link between Minaprine and Htr2a, though the exact nature of this relationship remains to be fully elucidated.",
